==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|fikil|lang=enm}}, {{term|fikil|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|ficol||fickle, cunning, tricky
, deceitful|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|fike|le}}. More at {{l|en|fike}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɪk.əl/}}, {{SAMPA|/fIk.@l/}}
*: {{audio|en-us-fickle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪkəl}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Quick to change one’s [[opinion]] or [[allegiance]]; [[insincere]]; not [[loyal]] or [[reliable]].

